**Syntax and calling:**

```java
interface CurrencyService {
    BigDecimal convert(String from, String to, BigDecimal amount);  // abstract

    // Static method — belongs to the INTERFACE, not implementations
    static BigDecimal roundToNearestPaisa(BigDecimal amount) {
        return amount.setScale(2, RoundingMode.HALF_UP);
    }

    static CurrencyService defaultService() {  // factory method
        return (from, to, amount) -> amount;    // identity — returns same amount
    }
}

// CORRECT: called via InterfaceName
BigDecimal rounded = CurrencyService.roundToNearestPaisa(new BigDecimal("123.456"));

// WRONG: cannot call via implementing class
// class ForexService implements CurrencyService { ... }
// ForexService.roundToNearestPaisa(...)  // COMPILE ERROR! Not inherited!

// WRONG: cannot call via instance
// ForexService forex = new ForexService();
// forex.roundToNearestPaisa(...)  // COMPILE ERROR!
```

**NOT inherited — proven with code:**

```java
interface Taxable {
    static BigDecimal gstRate() { return new BigDecimal("0.18"); }
}

class BrokerageService implements Taxable { }

// BrokerageService.gstRate();  // COMPILE ERROR! "cannot find symbol"
// Taxable.gstRate();           // WORKS! Returns 0.18
```

**CANNOT be overridden:**

```java
interface Taxable {
    static BigDecimal gstRate() { return new BigDecimal("0.18"); }
}

class BrokerageService implements Taxable {
    // This is NOT an override — it is a SEPARATE static method on the class
    // @Override  // COMPILE ERROR if you try @Override!
    static BigDecimal gstRate() { return new BigDecimal("0.12"); }
}

// Taxable.gstRate()          → 0.18 (interface's version)
// BrokerageService.gstRate() → 0.12 (class's own separate method, NOT override)
```

**Before vs After Java 8 — the utility class elimination:**

```java
// BEFORE Java 8: separate utility class + interface
interface Collection<E> { ... }
class Collections {  // utility class — just static methods
    static <T> void sort(List<T> list) { ... }
    static <T> List<T> unmodifiableList(List<T> list) { ... }
}

// AFTER Java 8: static methods ON the interface itself
interface List<E> extends Collection<E> {
    static <E> List<E> of(E... elements) { ... }     // Java 9
    static <E> List<E> copyOf(Collection<E> coll) { ... }  // Java 10
}
interface Map<K,V> {
    static <K,V> Map<K,V> of(K k, V v) { ... }
}
interface Comparator<T> {
    static <T,U> Comparator<T> comparing(Function<T,U> keyExtractor) { ... }
}
interface Predicate<T> {
    static <T> Predicate<T> not(Predicate<T> target) { ... }
}
```

**Common use cases for interface static methods:**

Factory methods: `List.of()`, `Map.of()`, `Predicate.not()`

Utility/helper: `Comparator.comparing()`, `Comparator.naturalOrder()`

Constants: `Taxable.gstRate()`

Validation: `AccountValidator.isValidIFSC(String code)`

